        "id": 53406,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-02-23T19:36:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>&gt;G claims that any three hero team can beat any villain on advanced mode.&nbsp; I've yet to give that a try, but I can definitely see some games being nigh unwinnable with certain three hero teams, ESPECIALLY against The Chairman.&nbsp; My group finds The Organization to be an absolute nightmare, so we don't play them as often as some of the other villains.&nbsp; Visionary is queen against The Organization, especially an early game Brain Burn.&nbsp; A Next Evolution/Lead From the Front combo with Legacy is nice as well, but there is less of a guarantee that he'll be able to get that combination out in time.&nbsp; Tempest's AoE is fantastic against them, especially through buffs and whittling down the Crooked Cops first to eliminate DR.</p><p>I haven't ever took on Advanced Organization with only three heroes, but I have always had great results with Visionary.&nbsp; Whoever you take, I recommend that she fills one of those slots.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
